WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.502
 Peter, Everett,
congratulations,

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.870
you fellas have made
it into the third round

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.471
of this competition.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.574
Now, when you came here,
we had you make signature

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.941
blades in your signature style.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.277
That's not going to happen
at your home forges.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.546
Instead, you'll be
making one of these--

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.450
Genghis Khan's sword.

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:19.719
 Sweet.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.753
 Good luck.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:22.155
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.155
 Bring your A game.

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:24.691
 I'll bring my A-plus game.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.558
 [laughs]

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:30.229 line:7%
[rock music]

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.931
 I'm back in Austin, Texas.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:35.769
And I have to make
Genghis Khan's sword.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.504
Let's get to work.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.506
I was considering
a Damascus build,

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:40.773
but I think that's a risk.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.011
You're asking for potential
delams and weak points.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.947
So I'm thinking of a
strong mono steel here.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.316
I'm going to go function,
function, function.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:52.051
I think that it's going to
be a challenge, no matter

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:53.853
what, just sheer length.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.187
You know, the longer
it is, it's harder

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:56.689
to keep these things straight.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:00.927
You're asking for warps and
other weirdness to go on.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.929
I'm hoping to get the
whole fuller in today

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.298
and the tang shaped out.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.434
I'm pretty happy with
how it's going so far.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:12.138
So basically, my sword
is ready to quench now.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.706
I pull it out.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.874
Wow, it's pretty straight.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.643
And it's hard.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.445
This is a huge relief.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.947 line:7%
[rock music]

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.415 line:7%
 So this is day 2.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.616 line:0%
It seems like day
10 or something.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:25.985
It's brutal.

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:27.186
I'm forging along.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.489
It's starting to
stretch out nicely.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.591
I want to leave it a little
bit thick to avoid a big--

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.726
[whoosh]

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.729
I should be able to get
into some heat treat.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.331
I really want to get this
done right the first time.

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.500
I don't want
something to go wrong.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.002
I pull it out--

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.103
not bad.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.304
Not like a pool stick.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:47.440
But it's got a little
whoop-de-doo in.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.842
But I've got a lot
of meat on the blade

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.944
to straighten that out.

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:54.380 line:7%
[rock music]

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:58.017 line:0%
 A little tired, but nothing
some good coffee won't cure.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.720
I got a octagonal
guard knocked out.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.322
And I'm going to make some
epoxy and set some pins,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.893
and then we'll start
thinking about our butt cap.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:11.498
My plan is to put this butt
guard on and use the press,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:15.067
just real gently, to conform
the metal over the groove,

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.436
and have it lock
into place so it's

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.705
got this physical connection.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.007
I go to the press.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:24.343
It feels like it should
just press into place.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:28.047
And then it
immediately goes south.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.048
Ah!

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.049
Crap.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.886
I break my freaking handle.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.954
It looks like I
popped it open there.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.522
I notice the
handle's screwed up,

00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:40.125
so I gotta pry it off, and clean
everything up, and re-epoxy,

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:41.861
re-pin everything.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.429
Round two.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.799
I also have to fix the butt
cap that I messed up trying

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.602
to press it into the tang.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.604
I have to change my
game plan and attach

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.673
the butt plate by epoxy.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.309
I do feel like I'll be able to
get a handle on the situation.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.577
[laughs]

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.713 line:7%
[rock music]

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.382
 I'm trying to figure
out this handle design.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.052
The finishing of
a weapon, I feel,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.221
is the most time consuming.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.488
This is tedious.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.991
So I got this curved
tang to deal with.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.627
So I decide to
cut the pieces up.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:18.131
My idea is to have
this tang sticking out,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.832
because I have to put
this little hole in there

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:20.800
for a little--

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.102
[whistles] little tassels.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.637
Put the handle together,
doing the dry fit.

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:26.905
Uh-oh.

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.841
See, my angle's way off.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.176
Hmm.

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.712
I'm going to go bend
this tang just a hair.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.314
It's gonna be real close.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.516
I really thought I'd
be further along, like,

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.785
pretty much done right now.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.888
But I think I'm set up good
for tomorrow to finish.

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.157 line:7%
[rock music]

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.492 line:7%
 It's the last day.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.626
I have a sword.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.262
So now, it's sharpen,
sharpen, sharpen.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.098
I'm going for a very sharp edge.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.734
And that's a bit of
a calculated risk.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:58.437
So it will certainly help in the
cut and potentially kill test.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:01.173
But if the strength
test is bashing

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.408
against bones or
something, then this

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:06.479
could be a detractor for me.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:10.282
I believe my sword is a lot like
Genghis Khan, actually-- sharp

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:12.285
and really frickin' brutal.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.286
I think there's only
one thing left to do.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.256
We've got to give this
some sort of test.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.362
Woo!

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.362
OK.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.497
That was kind of cool.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:29.769
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.805
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.907
I will take your sword
and deliver some killing

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:36.441
blows to this ballistics dummy.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.910
Peter, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:38.678
 Yes, sir.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.679
 Let's do this.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.648
[rock music]

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:46.953
[blade impacts]

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:57.964
[grunts]

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.969
 [chuckles]

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:11.143
 All right, Peter, first
up, your edge is sharp.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.711
The balance feels good.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:16.448
But it did take quite
a pronounced bend.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:21.754
But the more important
thing is, it will kill.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:22.989
I timed that perfectly.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.290
 [laughs]

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.291
 All right, Doc Everett,
are you ready, sir?

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.294
 Let's do some surgery.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.464
[rock music]

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:49.415
 Yikes.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:57.223
 All right, Everett,
your edge is very sharp.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:58.524
It slashes nicely.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.493
Your tip punctures easily.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.994
Cuts on the way out.

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:04.863
With all these cuts, it'll kill.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.632
 [laughs]

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.403
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.039
Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:15.140
of your blades,
I'll be attacking

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.042
our armored targets over here.

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:17.810
Peter, you're up first.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.245
You ready?

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.913
 Let her rip, tater chip.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.916
[rock music]

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.786
[blade impacts]

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.696
 All right, Peter.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.732
I'm gonna start
with your handle.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:43.202
I find it really comfortable the
way it flares towards the tip.

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.670
It works pretty
good for my hand.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.705
And I love what you
did with this kind

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:48.007
of low-layer count Damascus.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.675
It's very dramatic.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:55.915
But we've got some very
deep rolls on this edge.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.082
There they go.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:59.184
You hear it?

00:06:59.284 --> 00:07:00.886
Those chips, that's an issue.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:05.023
But all in all,
you did a good job.

00:07:05.123 --> 00:07:06.858
All right, Everett, you ready?

00:07:06.925 --> 00:07:07.660
 I am.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.326
 OK.

00:07:08.393 --> 00:07:11.831
[rock music]

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:20.205
 Ah, piece of armor.

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:23.109
[rock music]

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:27.713
 Nice.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:34.553
 All right, Everett,
your blade, still spot on.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.691
What I really like is
the fact that that blade

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:42.961
is, at its widest point,
maybe 3/16 of an inch.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:46.231
You don't need weight
and mass for strength

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:47.333
in a properly tempered blade.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.801
That's really good.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.770
You've got a section of
blade here that's not quite

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.905
as sharp as it was right there.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:55.775
All in all, I think
you did a great job.

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:57.076
 Awesome.

00:07:57.142 --> 00:08:01.080
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the war banner slice.

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:03.816
To test the sharpness of your
blade, I will take your weapon

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:06.285
and slash across
these war banners.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.786
Peter, you're up first.
You ready?

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:08.320
 Yes, sir.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.423
[rock music]

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:17.029
[blade impacts]

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.678
 So where your edge
has a chip, you can see,

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.214
it catches and rips
through the banner.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.683
Where it's not, it cuts nicely.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.886
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:42.187
All right, Everett,
it's your turn.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:43.589
You ready, sir?

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.290
 I think this beats the
hell out of peer review.

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:46.225
 All right, let's find out.

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:47.793
 [laughs]

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.062
[rock music]

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:56.602
[blade impacts]

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:08.346
 OK, Everett, your
edge here does cut.

00:09:08.413 --> 00:09:09.381
It's sharp.

00:09:09.447 --> 00:09:10.849
It cuts in some of the areas.

00:09:10.949 --> 00:09:12.718
On some parts of it, it ripped.

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:15.821
But overall, sir, it will cut.

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:17.189
 Awesome.

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:18.790
 All right, gentlemen, based on
what we've seen in the weapons

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:21.027
test, the judges have
made their final decision

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:23.229
about which of you is our
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:31.404
Peter, your sword took the most
damage in our strength test.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.739
You had a rolled edge,
and your blade bent.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:36.942
For that reason, I have to
dismiss you from the forge.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:39.544
Come on forward.

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:40.679
 I feel a little sad.

00:09:40.746 --> 00:09:44.650
But it's been an
awesome experience.

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:46.752
This loss is not
going to deter me.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.488
It's going to just
make me stronger.

00:09:49.588 --> 00:09:52.491
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.727
But I still think
I'm a badass smith.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:01.000
 Well, Everett, your blade
is comfortable, well-balanced,

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:02.201
strong, and deadly.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:03.935
And that makes you the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:06.172
And that's a title that comes
with a check for 10 grand.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.373
Good job.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:08.274
Come on forward and
shake our hands.

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:09.875
 [laughs]

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:11.643
This experience was really fun.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.778
It was really tough
in a lot of places.

00:10:13.878 --> 00:10:16.014
And it's been a hell of a ride.

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:19.285
[rock music]

